      "degree_level": "Bachelor, Master",
      "process_description": "Students in the IAKA’s Griechisch, Lateinisch and Mittellatein programmes may write theses; works are usually tied to a course (supervision by the course’s Dozierende; some proseminars also have tutors) but Bachelor (15 ECTS) and Master (30 ECTS) theses can be written without a course. Register/book the corresponding module (modules are normally booked in the semester after the associated course). Lengths: Bachelor 30–40 pages, Master 60–80 pages. Standard submission deadlines: 1 December (autumn) and 1 June (spring); if writing parallel to a course you must request permission by email to studium.klph@iaka.uzh.ch (deadlines then 6 Jan / 1 July). Submit an electronic PDF and usually a printed/Word copy; no post‑submission revisions; feedback only before submission. Extensions for medical reasons: up to one month with the supervisor or request module cancellation. Full formal rules and formatting are on the IAKA study pages (https://www.iaka.uzh.ch/de/klph/studium.html and subject subpages).",
